# Radiant Cut Halo Engagement Rings: 1ct Looks Like 1.5ct in Halo

Radiant cut halo engagement rings are the most visual-impact setting combination in diamond jewelry. A 1ct radiant cut sitting alone in a solitaire looks like a 1ct stone. Put that same 1ct radiant inside a single diamond halo and it reads like 1.4–1.5ct face-up.

That's not a trick. It's geometry. The rectangular halo frame adds diamond coverage on all four sides of the stone.

Combined with the radiant cut's 70-facet brilliance, the total face-up sparkle is higher per dollar than almost any other combination. The decision this post helps you make: single halo or double halo, which metal, which stones, and whether to add a pavé shank. Every price below is live certified market data with the ring total included.

**TL;DR:**
- Radiant cut halo engagement rings start at [$2,387 lab](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) or [$3,838 natural](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (stone + halo setting)
- A 1ct radiant in a single halo looks 30–40% larger face-up than a solitaire — highest size-multiplier of any fancy shape in a halo
- Single halo = center stone is the hero; double halo = the entire ring is the statement
- The halo's side diamonds are F-G color — your center stone should be F minimum in white gold
- → Best entry: [1ct E-VVS1 IGI lab, $867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Pavé Diamond Halo 14K WG, $1,520](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-cushion-emerald-radiant-by-james-allen-item-314929?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$2,387**

