> **Farzana says:** "Here's the thing people miss about halo rings: the side diamonds are usually F-G color. So if you put a G center stone in a white gold halo, the center can look slightly warmer than the halo. It's subtle — but it's there. Buy F minimum in white gold. In yellow gold, G is perfectly fine. The metal covers it."

