## Expert Summary

Radiant cut halo engagement rings are the highest value combination in diamond jewelry. No other shape-plus-setting gives you more apparent size per dollar than a radiant cut inside a single diamond halo. That's not marketing — it's the math of rectangular framing.

The size multiplier is real. A 1ct radiant in a solitaire looks like 1ct. The same stone in a single halo looks like 1.4–1.5ct. For a 1.5ct lab radiant, the halo puts the total visual footprint past 2ct.

You cannot buy that size in natural diamonds for anywhere near [$3,030](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

The single vs double halo decision matters more than most buyers realize. Single halo: the center stone is the hero. Double halo: the whole ring is the statement. If the cost of the second halo ring could instead size up your center stone, take the bigger stone every time.

More center stone + single halo beats smaller stone + double halo for almost every buyer.

Color grade is where halo buyers make mistakes. The halo diamonds are F-G. In white gold, a G center stone next to F halo diamonds looks slightly warm. Buy F minimum in white gold — and with lab stones, the price difference is small enough to make this a non-decision.

The [Pavé Diamond Halo specifically designed for radiant cuts at $1,520](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-cushion-emerald-radiant-by-james-allen-item-314929?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the right starting point for almost every buyer. Pair it with a 1ct E-VVS1 lab at [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and you have a ring that reads as a 1.5ct stone for [$2,387 total](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/pave-diamond-halo-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-cushion-emerald-radiant-by-james-allen-item-314929?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That is the core value proposition of the radiant cut halo.

For all radiant cut decisions beyond the halo, the [Radiant Cut Diamond: The Complete Buying Guide](https://diamondcritics.com/radiant-cut-diamond) covers every angle.
